  "verdict": "The earlier r3 4/4 result was a narrow two-scene, three-choice control and does not generalize to the expanded four-scene, four-choice suite. With byte-identical packed pixels and identical prompt counts, BF16 GPU scores 7/8, the executed NPU scores 4/8, and exact answers agree in 5/8 cases. The near-miss video is a realistic positive result at 2/2 in both normal and shuffled order, but broad GPU/NPU video-prediction parity remains unsolved. A 25-token prompt-compression diagnostic leaves NPU accuracy at 4/8 and persistent NPU-only box failures, so shorter wording is not a fix. A focused box-versus-near-miss test reaches NPU 3/4 and shows that the box can be recognized when listed first, narrowing the remaining failure to order sensitivity rather than total visual confusion."
